<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to May 31.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to May 31.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar  Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to May 31, (output in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week May 25-31</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97	 930,504 tns	 98,491 tns    10.58 pct</p>
<p>     95-96	 468,513 tns	 51,725 tns    11.04 pct</p>
<p>     94-95	 896,528 tns	 89,772 tns    10.01 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to May 31</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    40,627,490 tns    4,387,179 tns    10.80 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    39,596,746 tns    4,321,978 tns    10.91 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    38,906,395 tns    4,150,776 tns    10.67 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 42 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 25 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 39 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
